  "equivalent": true,
  "why": "EQUIVALENT, AND THE OBJECT SAYS WHY.  0x180 has its own rung at 0x6a668, tested three compares EARLIER in the chain -- `cmp $0x180,%dx; je 6a668` at 0x65567, before the `lea -0x41(%edx); cmp $0x13e,%ax; jbe 69995` at 0x65572 -- so the value can never reach this window whatever its upper bound is.  The object's own encoding of the bound is 0x13e, which is 0x17f - 0x41, and that IS pinned: `the lower window ends at 0x17e` and `the lower window starts at 0x40` are both caught.  What is untestable is only the one value the earlier rung already owns."
